    <!-- 2026-08-27: backend removed retail_sentiment/institutional_positioning/short_interest .description from Firestore ; these three replace them, verbatim from the backend team's own copy, and also back the new section-header info icons (previously only the top-level Positioning icon existed; these three sub-sections had none). -->
    <string name="positioning_retail_sentiment_description">Weekly AAII survey of individual investor sentiment. The bull-bear spread is a classic contrarian indicator — extreme optimism or pessimism among retail investors has historically preceded a reversal.</string>
    <string name="positioning_institutional_description">Speculative net futures positioning as a percentage of open interest, framed against a trailing ~1-year percentile per contract. A crowded long or short reading has historically preceded a reversal as that positioning unwinds — first-pass framing, not backtested. Reflects the prior Tuesday\'s book, not the report\'s Friday release date. ES/NQ/RTY use CFTC\'s Legacy non-commercial category; DIA uses TFF\'s Leveraged Funds category instead (Dow futures aren\'t reported under Legacy) — see each contract\'s own methodology before comparing DIA directly against the other three.</string>
    <string name="positioning_short_interest_description">FINRA-reported short interest in SPY/QQQ/IWM/DIA/RSP/MAGS as index/style-ETF proxies — not literal \'market short interest.\' Includes authorized-participant creation/redemption arbitrage flow, not purely directional bearish positioning. Settlement-date data, always roughly 8 business days stale by the time FINRA publishes it (see each instrument\'s settlement date vs. this gauge\'s fetched-at time).</string>
